  <!-- EN: Spain -->
  <BA_Spain_NobleHouse.label>西班牙</BA_Spain_NobleHouse.label>
  <!-- EN: Any man who is born on the Iberian Peninsula would call himself a "Spaniard", so when King Alfonso VI declared himself the "Emperor of all Spain" three years ago, it was a truly bold claim. After all, not since the times of the Western Roman Empire has one noble court truly ruled the peninsula unopposed. Currently, the Moors hold southern Iberia quite tightly, and Portugal's declaration of independence really proves Alfonso wrong.\n\n<i><color=#66E0E4FF>Medieval Kingdoms: Iberia</color></i> -->
  <BA_Spain_NobleHouse.description>任何出生在伊比利亚半岛的人都会自称“西班牙人”，因此三年前阿方索六世国王宣布自己为“全西班牙皇帝”时，这无疑是一份大胆的宣言。毕竟，自西罗马帝国时代以来，还没有哪个王室能真正无人反对地统治整个半岛。如今，摩尔人牢牢掌控着伊比利亚南部，而葡萄牙的独立宣言更是直接证明了阿方索的主张站不住脚。</BA_Spain_NobleHouse.description>
